('10808',NULL,'Envoy Proxy by OTLP','3','-1','2','','','Envoy Proxy by OTLP','0',NULL,'Envoy Proxy monitoring via OpenTelemetry (OTLP) traces and logs, using Zabbix''s native
APM Telemetry query items. Covers request volume, span error rate and duration
percentiles from Envoy''s OTel tracing integration, plus log severity counts.

Complements `Envoy Proxy by HTTP`, which covers Envoy''s own internal /stats metrics —
this template covers what /stats cannot: per-request span data.

Generated by official Zabbix template tool "Templator"','1','1','','','','','0','0','b1de7c3450834a4db51e654ece3142d4','ENVOY PROXY BY OTLP','Zabbix','8.0-1',NULL,'0','1','## Overview

This template collects Envoy Proxy''s OpenTelemetry (OTLP) traces and logs via Zabbix''s native
APM query items (Telemetry query), without external scripts or a Zabbix proxy script layer.

It complements `Envoy Proxy by HTTP` (which scrapes Envoy''s own `/stats` endpoint): that
template covers Envoy''s internal counters, this one covers per-request span data — request
volume, error rate, and latency percentiles — plus log severity counts.

## Setup

1. Enable Envoy''s OpenTelemetry tracing (or point an OpenTelemetry Collector in front of
   Envoy) at your Zabbix server/proxy''s OTLP endpoint. See
   https://www.envoyproxy.io/docs/envoy/latest/configuration/other_features/tracing#opentelemetry
2. Ensure the `TelemetryProvider` parameter is configured in the Zabbix server/proxy
   configuration file.
3. Apply the template to a host representing the Envoy instance.
4. Adjust the remaining macros (update interval, thresholds) if needed.

*Note: this template relies on Envoy''s own OpenTelemetry tracing integration — if your Envoy
build or configuration doesn''t export traces via OTLP, use `Envoy Proxy by HTTP` instead.*

For discussion, feedback, or improvements, please visit the Zabbix forum:
https://www.zabbix.com/forum/zabbix-suggestions-and-feedback'),
('10809',NULL,'OpenRouter traces by OTLP','3','-1','2','','','OpenRouter traces by OTLP','0',NULL,'OpenRouter template. Collects traces via APM query items and shows basic
span health indicators, durations, statuses, errors.
Note: OpenRouter sends completions traces only.

Generated by official Zabbix template tool "Templator"','1','1','','','','','0','0','b3fb25ec57b6424cbf0821bbb7e39a54','OPENROUTER TRACES BY OTLP','Zabbix','8.0-1',NULL,'0','1','## Overview
This template is designed to collect OpenRouter trace data. It provides a basic span overview
with health indicators, durations, statuses, errors.

## Setup
1. Ensure that OpenRouter account is configured to send traces to your OpenTelemetry collector.
    Each workspace requires separate configuration.
2. Ensure that the `TelemetryProvider` parameter is configured in the Zabbix server configuration file.
3. Apply the template to the host.
4. Adjust macros if needed.

### OpenRouter Configuration
OpenTelemetry Collector should configured in "Observability" menu in each workspace.
Endpoint configuration is enough.

*Note: OpenRouter sends completions traces only.*'),
('10810',NULL,'Generic OpenTelemetry by OTLP','3','-1','2','','','Generic OpenTelemetry by OTLP','0',NULL,'This template collects OpenTelemetry (OTLP) telemetry — traces, metrics and logs — via Zabbix''s native APM query items (Telemetry query), without external scripts
or a Zabbix proxy script layer. It works with any OTLP-instrumented application or with an OpenTelemetry Collector in front of it.

Generated by official Zabbix template tool "Templator"','1','1','','','','','0','0','8180057720eb426aa7ddfc6e755a51a3','GENERIC OPENTELEMETRY BY OTLP','Zabbix','8.0-1',NULL,'0','1','## Overview

This template collects OpenTelemetry (OTLP) telemetry — traces, metrics and logs — via Zabbix''s native APM query items (Telemetry query), without external scripts
or a Zabbix proxy script layer. It works with any OTLP-instrumented application or with an OpenTelemetry Collector in front of it.

### What is monitored

- **Traces**: span counts and durations grouped by status code (Ok / Error / Unset), and the derived span error rate.
- **Metrics**: metric point counts.
- **Logs**: log record counts grouped by severity band.

### Requirements

- A Zabbix server/proxy build with APM (OTLP) ingestion enabled and reachable by your
  instrumented application or OpenTelemetry Collector.
- The application, service, or collector must be configured to export via OTLP to that endpoint.

## Setup

1. Point your application''s OpenTelemetry SDK (or an OpenTelemetry Collector in front of it) at your Zabbix server/proxy''s OTLP endpoint.
2. Apply this template to a host representing the instrumented application or service.
3. Adjust the interval macros if the defaults don''t match how often your
   source actually emits data.
4. Adjust thresholds macros.

For discussion, feedback, or improvements, please visit the Zabbix forum:
https://www.zabbix.com/forum/zabbix-suggestions-and-feedback'),
('10811',NULL,'Proxmox VE by OTLP','3','-1','2','','','Proxmox VE by OTLP','0',NULL,'Proxmox VE node monitoring over OpenTelemetry telemetry stored in ClickHouse.
Requires a metric server of the OpenTelemetry (OTLP) type configured in Proxmox VE; every item is a direct Telemetry query filtered by service and metric name.

Generated by official Zabbix template tool "Templator"','1','1','','','','','0','0','866dc6d0116844298052ae62af0b99f3','PROXMOX VE BY OTLP','Zabbix','8.0-1',NULL,'0','1','## Overview

The template monitors a Proxmox VE node from its OpenTelemetry metric stream stored in the APM (ClickHouse) backend, using Telemetry query items.
It covers the node itself: CPU, load, memory, swap, ZFS ARC, root filesystem and uptime.

## Setup

1. In the Proxmox VE web interface, add a metric server of the OpenTelemetry (OTLP) type (`Datacenter` > `Metric Server` > `Add` > `OpenTelemetry`) and point it at your OTLP collector.
2. Make sure the OTLP collector exports the received metrics into the ClickHouse database (service name `proxmox-ve`).
3. Configure `TelemetryProvider` on Zabbix server/proxy to point at that ClickHouse database.
4. Link the template to a host.'),
