('71592','15','','10817','Calculated value of innodb_log_file_size','percona.innodb_log_file_size','1m','31d','365d','0','0','','','','',NULL,NULL,'(last(//percona.innodb_os_log_written) - last(//percona.innodb_os_log_written,#1:now-1h)) / {$PERCONA.INNODB_LOG_FILES}','','0','','','','','0',NULL,'`Innodb_log_file_size` is calculated as: (`innodb_os_log_written`-`innodb_os_log_written`(time shift -1h))/`{$PERCONA.INNODB_LOG_FILES}`. `Innodb_log_file_size` is the size in bytes of each InnoDB redo log file in the log group. The combined size can be no more than 512 GB. Larger values mean less disk I/O due to less flushing checkpoint activity, but also slower recovery from a crash.','0','7d','0','',NULL,'','','','','200','1','0','','','0','0','0','0','0','0','0','fc75ec111605455fa1d75f9db82cea63','0','2','0','{}','15s','10m','15s','0'),
