('9303','1','39','Filters','Filter for services that must not run','Regex string to match the services that are expected to stay stopped. Such services are discovered regardless of their startup type and raise a problem when they are running.','0','',''),
('9304','1','40','Thresholds','Grace period after boot for services','Services with the "automatic delayed" startup type may legitimately stay stopped for a while after a reboot. The "is not running" trigger is suppressed until the system uptime exceeds this value.','0','^[0-9]+[smhd]?$',''),
('9305','1','37','Filters','Filter for service by start trigger','Regex string to include discovered service by its start trigger flag: `1` for services configured for Trigger Start, `0` otherwise.','0','',''),
('9306','1','38','Filters','Filter for service by start trigger (exclude)','Regex string to exclude discovered service by its start trigger flag. By default Trigger Start services are excluded: they are started on demand and stop normally when idle.','0','',''),
